PROBLEM: Login succeeded server-side (logs showed 'SUCESSO: sessão emitida')
but the user was redirected back to /login. The session cookie was not
persisting in the browser.

ROOT CAUSE: All 4 auth API routes (login, setup, setup-admin, logout) were
setting the session cookie via response.headers.set('Set-Cookie', ...).
On Next.js 16.1.x with a custom server (server.js), this approach is
unreliable — the Set-Cookie header can be silently dropped during
response processing, so the browser never receives it.

FIX:
- Added setSessionCookie() / clearSessionCookie() helpers in src/lib/auth.ts
  that use response.cookies.set({...}) — the Next.js 16 recommended API.
- Updated all 4 auth routes to use the new helpers.
- Added debug logging in middleware (logs when cookie is missing or JWT
  invalid, including which cookie names ARE present).
- Added debug logging in /api/auth/me (logs cookie presence + verification
  result).
- Added explicit credentials: 'same-origin' to fetch calls in /login and
  /admin pages (belt-and-suspenders; this is the default but now explicit).
- Bumped version to v7.27 in package.json, login page, admin page, and
  main page sidebar.

The legacy buildSessionCookieHeader() / buildClearSessionCookieHeader()
functions are kept because auth-edge.cjs (used by server.js for socket.io
auth) still needs the raw Set-Cookie string format.
